      "value": "@{5b2821f1443b6a55287c67ad|full_name}: Tupper - \"Shut down VRChat. Press your Windows key and type \"cmd\" into your Windows Search bar. Right click \"Command Prompt\" and click \"Run as Administrator\". A black command prompt window should pop up. Copy this command with Ctrl-C, and paste it into the window by right-clicking in the window.\n\nREG DELETE HKCU\\Software\\VRChat\\vrchat /va\n\nPress Y when asked to confirm, and then press Enter. After you're done, close the window and try VRChat again.\"\n\nDoing that will get you into the tutorial world but you still can't join friends or other worlds...\n\n If you do the REG DELETE then join friends from the VrChat website (BEFORE opening VrChat) you will be able to join friends and/or other worlds. It will bring you to the login page. After logging in you will get the Login Loop a couple of times but it should eventually bring up the world loading screen.\n\n*Keep in mind you will have to do all those steps every time you want to change worlds.*",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
